   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2016, CDC invested $20 million into AFIG II, alongside the EIB, the African Development Bank, and other European DFIs including Germany&#x2019;s DEG and Sweden&#x2019;s SwedFund. The fund targets investments of between $5 million to $20 million and the fund manager is aiming for a total fund size of $170 million.Our investment provides growth capital to support the sustainable expansion of small firms in Central, East and West African countries.</narrative>
   </description>
